git/views
# @summary The mirrors' directory under the home, the same path on the host and in every view: 'guest repo add' keeps a bare mirror of each repository a guest gets there (VM_BAKE_REPO_VIEWS/<name>, <name> the last element of the repository's path), and the template's home line 'template home add <template> git/views' hangs it read-only into the views -- the guest clones and pulls from the mirrors and can change nothing in them, not a hook, not a config. A path relative to the home; the host's directory must exist before 'guest start' (guest check homes), 'guest repo add' makes it.
